# Windsurf Rules for Destilado Digital PWA

## General Rules
- Maximum 500 lines per file
- Follow YAGNI principle: implement only what's needed now
- Use TypeScript for all components
- Use TailwindCSS for styling
- Use shadcn/ui components when available

## Code Structure
- Keep files focused and single-purpose
- Use descriptive variable and function names
- Add comments only when necessary
- Prefer functional components with hooks

## File Organization
- /app - Next.js app router pages
- /lib - Utility functions and configurations
- /components - Reusable UI components
- /types - TypeScript type definitions

## Import Order
1. React and Next.js imports
2. External library imports
3. Internal imports (lib, components, types)

## Styling Guidelines
- Use TailwindCSS classes only
- Avoid inline styles
- Use semantic HTML elements
- Ensure responsive design by default

## Database Rules
- Use Supabase for data persistence
- Environment variables for configuration
- Type-safe database interactions

## Performance
- Optimize images and assets
- Use Next.js built-in optimizations
- Implement lazy loading where appropriate

## Security
- Validate all user inputs
- Use environment variables for secrets
- Implement proper authentication flows
